    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Hold is implemented, but `bin/e2e` doesn't fully pass: 3 of the 4 tests pass and \"hold scenario 3\" fails. It fails at line 454, a `ui.refresh(pg_uma)` call that comes before any of that test's hold checks.\n\n**Why it fails:** uma's page still shows Cam when wes retires Cam (line 452). When uma's page reloads, Cam is correctly hidden because \"Show retired\" is off. But the `refresh` helper in `e2e/support/ui.ts` waits for every row that was on screen before to come back, so it times out. Line 461 of the same test then expects Cam to be hidden on uma's page. Those two can't both hold with the app's current retire behaviour, and hold isn't involved. I'm not allowed to edit the spec or the helper, and I didn't want to fudge how retired people are shown just to get past it, so I left it.\n\n**Checking the rest:** I ran a temporary copy of the spec with only line 454 changed: it turns \"Show retired\" on for that one refresh, then off again. With that change all 4 tests pass, including every hold figure and the full audit sequence. I deleted the copy; the original spec is untouched.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Stored data:** a new migration, `V18__person_held.sql`, adds a `held` flag to each person (default off).\n- **Server:**\n  - A new `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/people/{id}/hold` toggles hold. It writes `PERSON_HELD name=<name>` or `PERSON_RELEASED name=<name>`, followed by the usual ROLLUP and TOTALS lines for any figures that moved.\n  - `RollupService` no longer counts a held person's OPEN claims in their figures, the sheet's totals, or a period's due-total (which is what gets fixed when a period closes). SETTLED claims still count.\n- **Front end (`people.ts`, `people-api.ts`):**\n  - Each person row has a `person-hold` cell showing yes or no, and a `person-hold-toggle` button labelled Hold or Release.\n  - The screen's totals apply the same rule as the server: claimed, due-total, the sheet totals and period totals.\n\nOne judgement call: I didn't change how statements work. A statement taken for a held person still includes their OPEN claims, because I read a statement as a snapshot rather than a live total. The tests don't cover this case.",
